CC(1)

NAME
     cc - the C compiler

SYNOPSIS
     cc [-c | -S | -E] [-o file] [-Idir] [-Dname[=value]] [-Uname]
        [-Ldir] [-lname] [-s] [-v] [-w] file...

DESCRIPTION
     cc compiles C programs for AZ/UX. Files ending in .c are compiled,
     .s files are assembled, and .o and .a files are passed to the
     linker. Unless -c, -S or -E is given, everything is linked with
     /usr/lib/crt0.o and /usr/lib/libc.a into a.out (or -o file).

     The compiler (azcc) implements most of C99: all the integer types
     including long long, float and double (on the 68882), structures,
     unions and bit-fields, enumerations, typedefs, function pointers,
     variadic functions (<stdarg.h>), designated and nested
     initializers, compound literals, static assertions, inline
     assembly statements (asm("...") without operands) and the GNU
     statement-expression and typeof extensions. Not supported: complex
     numbers, variable-length arrays and wide-character library
     functions.

     Types: char 8 bits (signed), short 16, int and long 32, long long
     64, pointers 32; float and double are IEEE single and double.

OPTIONS
     -c         compile or assemble only; write file.o
     -S         compile only; write file.s (azas assembly)
     -E         preprocess only, to standard output (or -o)
     -o file    name the output
     -I dir     search dir for #include files (before /usr/include)
     -D n[=v]   define a macro;  -U n   undefine one
     -L dir     search dir for libraries;  -l name   link libname.a
     -s         strip the symbol table
     -v         say what is being done
     -w         suppress warnings
     -O, -g, -W..., -f..., -m..., -std=...   accepted and ignored

     Predefined macros include __STDC__, __STDC_VERSION__ (199901L),
     __m68k__, __mc68030__, __HAVE_68881__, __AZUX__, __unix__ and
     __azcc__.

CALLING CONVENTION
     Arguments are pushed right to left in 4-byte slots (long long and
     double take 8); the caller removes them. Results return in d0 (and
     a0 for pointers), d0:d1 for long long, fp0 for floating point.
     d2-d7, a2-a6 and fp2-fp7 are preserved. C names get a leading
     underscore in assembly (main is _main).

FILES
     /usr/include, /usr/lib/libc.a, /usr/lib/crt0.o

SEE ALSO
     as(1), ld(1), ar(1), make(1), intro(3)
